# Application

Application guides own the process-level model: the generated host, direct builder control, startup and shutdown, and the one-protocol runtime invariant. They do not define HTTP, WebSocket, or RPC wire behavior.

## Choose a task

| Task | Guide |
|---|---|
| let Upwell own `main`, CLI setup, and tooling discovery | <GuideRef slug="framework/application/app-macro">The `app!` macro</GuideRef> |
| acquire resources, roll back startup, and drain shutdown | <GuideRef slug="framework/application/lifecycle">Lifecycle and graceful shutdown</GuideRef> |
| run HTTP, RPC, jobs, or custom protocols as deliberate hosts | <GuideRef slug="framework/application/protocol-composition">Protocol composition</GuideRef> |

## Shared prerequisites

Start with the <GuideRef slug="framework">application model</GuideRef>. Decide whether Upwell owns the process boundary before adding hooks or multiple hosts, and keep reusable dependencies in <GuideRef slug="framework/dependency-injection">dependency injection</GuideRef> rather than global process state.
